---
/**
 * The small accented line above a headline. On the home page it names the site,
 * on an entity page it names what you are looking at, which is the one thing
 * the big name itself cannot tell you: "Chain Reaction" is both a label and two
 * unrelated artists.
 *
 * 0.8125rem rather than 0.75, to match the `LabelledBand` heading. The two are
 * the only mono type on the site that heads something rather than captioning
 * it, so they read at one size: an eyebrow naming the page and a band label
 * naming a section are the same job at two altitudes.
 *
 * On a phone it steps down to 0.6875rem. At 0.32em of tracking the full size
 * eats most of a narrow viewport and starts competing with the name below it,
 * which is the one thing an eyebrow must not do.
 */
---

<p class="text-accent font-mono text-[0.6875rem] md:text-[0.8125rem] tracking-[0.32em] uppercase"><slot /></p>
